<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="idb8c69599-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8" identifier="/us/usc/t18/s341"><ns0:num value="341">§ 341.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Definitions</ns0:heading><ns0:content>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">As used in this chapter, the term “common carrier” means a locomotive, a rail carrier, a sleeping car carrier, a bus transporting passengers in interstate commerce, a water common carrier, and an air common carrier.</ns0:p>
</ns0:content><ns0:sourceCredit id="idb8c6959a-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">(Added <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/99/570/tI/s1971/a">Pub. L. 99–570, title I, § 1971(a)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1986-10-27">Oct. 27, 1986</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/100/3207-59">100 Stat. 3207–59</ns0:ref>; amended <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/100/690/tVI/s6482/a">Pub. L. 100–690, title VI, § 6482(a)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1988-11-18">Nov. 18, 1988</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/102/4382">102 Stat. 4382</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
